left-to-right order of the leaves gives a consecutive-ones arrangement of the columns. So does
the result of reversing the leaf descendants of a node. The order of leaves of a consecutive
set of children of a P node can also be reversed to obtain a new consecutive-ones ordering.
All consecutive-ones orderings can be obtained by a sequence of these reversals.
